<Project Sdk="Assimalign.Cohesion.Sdk.Database">
	<!--
		A plain Database program: no platform or application-model package, and no code of the hub's runtime.

		[proposed] in v2 (§8.4; §15, decision 46): the hub's database package, under its advisory name. It declares
		identity's whole database and ships the extension that Program.cs calls. It references Database.Sql and never
		IdentityHub.Hosting. It stands where the orders and users database projects reference their domain library.

		The image of this project (bookstore-identity-database) changes when this project or the Cohesion version
		does. A new schema of identity arrives with a new version of the package, and this program's engine applies
		it at start. A release of the hub alone never restarts the database.

		Untested (v2 §8.3): Sdk.Database reads schema declarations from a project's own source, and this project has
		none. A build stops with COHDBSDK101 only when a project sets CohesionDatabaseProject to true. This one does
		not, so it builds, and it has no schema artifact for the hub's database.
	-->
	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.IdentityHub.Sql.Schema" Version="$(CohesionVersion)" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
